    "prerequisite_note": "Review requirements, acceptance outcomes and test-design oracles before selecting functional assertions.",
    "practice": "What is a functional oracle based on?|Required behavior|Only current output|Only code style|Only test speed|A functional check needs an intended-behavior basis independent of the observed result.|Current output can be wrong;Style is not feature behavior;Speed does not define expected behavior.\nA request returns success. What may still need checking?|Relevant state effects|Only response branding|Only issue age|Only method names|Transport success may coexist with missing or incorrect required effects.|Branding does not inspect state;Age is not behavior;Private names are not user outcomes.\nA cancellation case starts with an already cancelled order. What should be clarified?|The intended scenario|That all cancellations fail|That the tool is broken|That setup never matters|The initial state determines whether the case checks a first cancellation or repeated action.|One state is not universal;No tool failure is established;Preconditions affect the oracle.\nA job is queued for a refund. Which claim is too strong?|Money was reversed|The request was accepted|A job identifier exists|The fixture returned a status|Queue acceptance does not establish completion of an external financial effect.|Acceptance can be observed;A returned identifier can exist;The status observation is scoped evidence.\nA test asserts an undocumented JSON key order. What is the risk?|Incidental coupling|Guaranteed contract coverage|Proven all-client safety|Improved business oracle|Unpromised representation details can cause brittle failures unrelated to the intended contract.|An extra assumption is not contract evidence;Client scope remains bounded;Ordering does not define the business rule.\nA functional case covers one eligible order. What remains limited?|Scenario scope|Its observed state|Its declared actor|Its fixture input|One selected case cannot establish every state, actor or failure sequence.|The state can be observed;The actor can be declared;The input is known.",
    "formal": "What is functional testing primarily about?|Specified outcomes|Only internal naming|Only execution duration|Only deployment frequency|Functional evidence compares operations and effects with required behavior.|Names are implementation detail;Duration is a separate property;Frequency does not establish correctness.\nWhy inspect the initial state?|It changes the rule context|It guarantees root cause|It replaces assertions|It eliminates failure paths|The same action can have different expected results in different states.|Context does not diagnose cause;An oracle is still required;Other paths remain relevant.\nWhat distinguishes accepted from completed work?|The operation outcome|Only response length|Only a ticket label|Only a function name|Asynchronous acceptance and eventual effect are different observable states.|Length does not prove effect;Labels need semantic evidence;Names do not establish completion.\nA retailer cancels an order but inventory never returns. What should tests examine?|The required side effect|Only the success banner|Only source formatting|Only the endpoint spelling|Cancellation requirements can include inventory effects beyond the immediate response.|A banner can mask state errors;Style is not effect evidence;Spelling alone does not establish semantics.\nAn LMS enrollment API returns another learner\u2019s details after success. What belongs in functional evidence?|Permitted response scope|Only a 200 status|Only a new button label|Only a shorter payload|Required behavior includes which data is allowed in the response.|Status alone does not establish scope;Labels do not restrict fields;Smaller can still be unauthorized.\nA bank tests expected fees by calling the same production function twice. What is weak?|Oracle independence|Only test duration|Only case grouping|Only report storage|A shared erroneous computation can agree with itself without validating the requirement.|Time is not independence;Grouping does not repair the oracle;Storage is unrelated to expected-value authority.\nA hospital appointment case uses an unauthorized actor but expects success. What needs review?|Scenario preconditions|Only assertion syntax|Only browser version|Only method naming|The actor\u2019s permission context affects the correct result.|Syntax can be valid with a wrong oracle;Version is not the stated issue;Names do not grant permission.\nA logistics feature promises eventual processing but a test demands immediate final state. What must be aligned?|The timing contract|Only screenshot size|Only branch age|Only log colors|The oracle must reflect specified asynchronous timing rather than invent a synchronous guarantee.|Images do not define timing;Age is unrelated;Colors do not establish completion.\nA SaaS test breaks when harmless response fields reorder. What should be considered?|An unnecessary assertion|A proven business defect|A required release rollback|A guaranteed client outage|If ordering is not promised or relied on, the test may assert incidental representation details.|Not every difference violates behavior;Rollback needs relevant risk evidence;Client impact is not automatically established.\nA university checks calculation, persistence and permitted response on an isolated fixture. What is defensible?|Those scoped outcomes passed|Every deployment is correct|Every external effect completed|All possible states were covered|The result supports the actual exercised outcomes under its declared fixture and boundaries.|Environment applicability is limited;External effects may be substituted;Selected cases are not exhaustive."
