    "prerequisite_note": "Use API Security object-level permission concepts and test-design controlled preconditions.",
    "practice": "What should a negative case include?|A defined rejection oracle|Only an invalid label|Only random characters|Only a guessed exception|The case must specify how disallowed conditions should be handled and what must remain unchanged.|A label does not define behavior;Randomness lacks an oracle;A guessed error may not match the contract.\nWhy vary one relevant invalid condition at a time?|Avoid masking controls|Prove every input|Guarantee a known cause|Remove setup requirements|One earlier rejection can prevent a later validation or permission boundary from being exercised.|Selected cases are not exhaustive;A failure does not automatically diagnose cause;Valid setup is still needed.\nA cross-owner case uses invalid JSON. What remains unproven?|Object authorization|That parsing rejected|That input was malformed|The local response status|Parsing may reject before the permission check is reached.|Parsing failure can be observed;The input format is known;Status can be recorded.\nWhat should accompany a denied write check?|Unchanged protected state|Only a new error color|Only faster execution|Only a shorter message|Denial should not conceal a mutation that already occurred.|Appearance does not inspect state;Speed does not establish atomic denial;Message length is not integrity evidence.\nA negative case expects a stack trace in public output. What needs review?|Disclosure policy|Only test naming|Only report order|Only field width|Useful public errors should not unnecessarily expose sensitive implementation details.|Names do not govern disclosure;Ordering is unrelated;Width does not define the error contract.\nA tester wants real accounts to check cross-owner denial. What is appropriate?|Isolated synthetic actors|Unapproved public probing|Shared student credentials|A broad production export|Authorized isolated fixtures can challenge permission rules without accessing real private records.|Public probing exceeds the scope;Shared credentials undermine accountability;A full export is unnecessary.",
    "formal": "What can negative testing examine?|Disallowed conditions|Only successful operations|Only code formatting|Only release cadence|Negative cases assess specified behavior when input, authority or state is not permitted.|Success is a different case;Style is not rejection behavior;Cadence does not define the oracle.\nWhat makes a rejection case meaningful?|It reaches the intended control|Any earlier error suffices|A red status badge suffices|An exception always proves safety|The setup should exercise the boundary the case claims to test.|Earlier checks may mask it;A badge is not mechanism evidence;Exceptions can occur after harmful effects.\nWhy assert absence of mutation?|Protect state integrity|Guarantee all privacy rules|Replace the response oracle|Prove every race condition|A rejected write must not produce the forbidden state change in the checked case.|Privacy needs other evidence;Response behavior still matters;A local case does not establish all concurrency.\nAn LMS malformed payload gets 400 on another student\u2019s record. What cannot be concluded?|Ownership enforcement|The observed parse rejection|The supplied target ID|That a response occurred|The request may fail before object-level authorization is evaluated.|Parse rejection is scoped evidence;The target can be known;The response is observed.\nA retailer rejects an invalid quantity but decrements stock first. What is wrong?|A forbidden mutation|Only the error caption|Only response duration|Only a test identifier|Rejecting the request does not justify leaving an unauthorized or invalid mutation.|Caption changes do not repair state;Timing is not the core discrepancy;IDs are unrelated.\nA bank tests expired identity with a valid operation. What should be checked?|Denial and protected effects|Only a success response|Only parsing validity|Only a screenshot of login|The operation should not gain authority or mutate protected state with invalid identity.|Success contradicts the intended negative case;Parsing alone omits identity;A login image does not inspect the operation.\nA hospital combines wrong actor, bad JSON and invalid state in one case. What needs supplementing?|Isolated boundary cases|Only a longer message|Only another combined case|Only a larger screenshot|Separate controlled cases can reveal which protections are actually reached and effective.|Length does not improve coverage;Another combined error can mask controls;Image size is not evidence breadth.\nA logistics error reveals private shipment existence to unauthorized users. What should be reviewed?|Error information exposure|Only status-code count|Only the tooltip wording|Only test sort order|The public rejection contract should not disclose protected facts unnecessarily.|Counts do not establish content safety;A tooltip may omit API disclosure;Ordering is irrelevant.\nA SaaS case triggers a server exception and calls it secure rejection. What is missing?|Response and state oracle|Only an exception counter|Only a test color|Only a shorter timeout|A crash does not prove intentional safe denial or absence of harmful effects.|Counts do not define correctness;Colors are not evidence;Timeout length does not inspect state.\nA university uses synthetic tenants to test forbidden exports. What should the report claim?|The exercised boundary result|Every live tenant inspected|All deployments safe|No remaining access risks|Isolated cases provide relevant but bounded evidence about selected rules and paths.|Synthetic fixtures do not inspect all real accounts;Configuration may differ;Untested paths may remain."
