    "prerequisite_note": "Use test plans and traceability to judge whether maintenance removes duplication or meaningful evidence.",
    "practice": "What makes a regression case worth retaining?|Relevant evidence|Only its age|Only its long runtime|Only its large assertion count|A case should challenge a meaningful current obligation or failure mechanism.|Old cases can become obsolete;Cost is not value by itself;Many weak assertions can add little evidence.\nA requirement is retired. What should happen to its assertion?|Review its oracle and scope|Keep it as current truth|Delete every related case|Mark it passed without running|Maintenance should assess whether the test is obsolete or still covers another relevant distinction.|A retired rule is not automatically current;Related cases may still matter;Results require actual evidence.\nA test depends on private field ordering not promised by the API. What is fragile?|Incidental coupling|The existence of an oracle|All integration testing|The use of automation|Unspecified implementation details can change without violating the contract.|Oracles remain necessary;Integration can be useful;Automation is not the cause by itself.\nTwo similarly titled tests use different actors. What should be checked before merging?|Actor-boundary coverage|Only title length|Only execution speed|Only the author initials|Different actors can exercise different authorization boundaries despite similar names.|Length does not define scope;Speed is not equivalence;Authors do not determine behavior.\nA failure is removed only to make CI green. What is missing?|A reasoned disposition|A faster pipeline|A smaller report|A new ticket label|The team must determine whether the failure is a defect, obsolete rule or test problem.|Speed does not justify suppression;Size is not rationale;Labels do not resolve meaning.\nA suite case has no clear purpose. What is appropriate?|Investigate its claim|Automatically trust it|Delete all neighbors|Treat it as full coverage|The oracle and relevance should be understood before accepting or removing the evidence.|Unclear cases are not authority;Other cases may be valid;One unclear case cannot cover everything.",
